  {"type": "split", "h2": "AC repair or replace: how we help you decide", "image": "Parent and child relaxing in a cool, comfortable home", "image_src": "/assets/img/brands/lennox-home-comfort.webp", "image_fit": "cover", "image_pos": "50% 50%", "image_credit": "Image: Lennox", "html": "<p>If your central air conditioner is under 10 years old and the fix is a capacitor, contactor, fan motor or drain, repair it. Those are routine, and the unit has plenty of life left.</p><p>If the unit is 12 to 15 years old and the quote is for a compressor, an evaporator coil or a major refrigerant leak, think hard. The repair can run a third or more of a new system, and the old unit will still have its old efficiency.</p><p>At that point a <a href=\"/heat-pump/\">cold-climate heat pump</a> deserves a look. It cools like an AC, takes over most of your heating, and a qualifying model can return up to $7,500 through the Home Renovation Savings Program. A plain <a href=\"/ac/\">air conditioner replacement</a> is still the right call for some homes, and we quote both without pressure.</p>"},
